{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "The scale scenarios stop at 50K. 50K already separates the targets on",
    "every axis these scenarios exist to measure — accept-queue drain rate,",
    "flow-table cost, per-connection memory, and datagram loss under a",
    "receive-buffer bound — so 100K only bought a longer run, not a different",
    "verdict. It cost roughly half the wall clock of a full profile and put",
    "the load generator, not the proxy, at the ephemeral-port and descriptor",
    "ceiling, which measures the harness rather than the target.",
    "Raise the ceiling in scripts/collect.py and scripts/preflight.sh before",
    "reintroducing a larger size."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "warmup_seconds": 2,
    "duration_seconds": 10,
    "repetitions": 3,
    "connect_timeout_ms": 5000,
    "stable_error_rate": 0.001
  },
